<!DOCTYPE article PUBLIC "-//NLM//DTD Journal Archiving and Interchange DTD v2.3 20070202//EN" "archivearticle.dtd"><article xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" article-type="correction"><?properties open_access?><front><journal-meta><journal-id journal-id-type="nlm-ta">J Cell Biol</journal-id><journal-id journal-id-type="publisher-id">jcb</journal-id><journal-title>The Journal of Cell Biology</journal-title><issn pub-type="ppub">0021-9525</issn><issn pub-type="epub">1540-8140</issn><publisher><publisher-name>The Rockefeller University Press</publisher-name></publisher></journal-meta><article-meta><article-id pub-id-type="pmc">2600756</article-id><article-id pub-id-type="publisher-id">20071111220081120c</article-id><article-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1083/jcb.20071111220081120c</article-id><article-categories><subj-group subj-group-type="heading"><subject>Corrections</subject><subj-group><subject>Correction</subject></subj-group></subj-group></article-categories><title-group><article-title>Quantitative analysis of autophagy-related protein stoichiometry by fluorescence microscopy</article-title></title-group><contrib-group><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Geng</surname><given-names>Jiefei</given-names></name></contrib><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Baba</surname><given-names>Misuzu</given-names></name></contrib><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Nair</surname><given-names>Usha</given-names></name></contrib><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Klionsky</surname><given-names>Daniel J.</given-names></name></contrib></contrib-group><pub-date pub-type="ppub"><day>15</day><month>12</month><year>2008</year></pub-date><volume>183</volume><issue>6</issue><fpage>1175</fpage><lpage>1175</lpage><permissions><copyright-statement>Copyright &#x000a9; 2008, The Rockefeller University Press</copyright-statement></permissions><self-uri xlink:title="pdf" xlink:href="jcb1831175.pdf"/></article-meta></front><body><p>Vol. 182 No. 1, July 14, 2008. Pages <related-article related-article-type="corrected-article" vol="182" page="129" id="N0x1c871c0N0x399f430" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="18625846" ext-link-type="pubmed">129&#x02013;140</related-article>.</p><p>In Table I, &#x0201c;272 &#x000b1; 9&#x0201d; is reported as the number of Atg8 molecules at the PAS, but this value refers to starvation conditions. For growing conditions, the correct amount of Atg8 at the PAS is 116 &#x000b1; 7 molecules. Similarly, in Fig. 6 A, the boxplot showing the amount of Atg8 at the PAS refers to starvation conditions. The authors apologize for this error and for any inconvenience.</p></body></article>